{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba .github/workflows/version-pr.yml'","aggregated_output":"     1\tname: version-pr\n     2\t# The ADR-0325 version PR — the ONLY place changesets are consumed. Operator-dispatched; authors\n     3\t# a branch carrying the WHOLE release source truth as one reviewable PR: `changeset version`\n     4\t# (package.json bumps + CHANGELOGs + consumed .changeset/*.md), a refreshed bun.lock, the ledger\n     5\t# append, the index.json rebuild, and the tarballs.json hash rows (packed here so the publish leg\n     6\t# can later re-pack at the release tag and byte-verify — `bun pm pack` is deterministic for\n     7\t# identical source bytes).\n     8\t#\n     9\t# Flow (ADR-0325, amends ADR-0318/0223 mechanics):\n    10\t#   1. operator dispatches THIS workflow → it opens the version PR\n    11\t#   2. operator merges it → push-to-main CI (the 5 required checks) runs on the merge commit\n    12\t#   3. operator publishes a GitHub Release whose tag targets EXACTLY that merge commit\n    13\t#   4. release-train.yml readiness re-verifies (CI green at the tag SHA, changesets drained,\n    14\t#      tag-on-main) → propagation legs publish exactly the tagged bytes, zero source mutation\n    15\t#\n    16\t# The initial branch push uses the ephemeral GITHUB_TOKEN, so it does NOT trigger pull_request CI\n    17\t# (GitHub anti-loop rule). Later operator pushes do trigger the synchronize lane below: it re-packs\n    18\t# every row introduced since the branch fork point and commits any changed bytes back to the release\n    19\t# branch. Historical rows from main stay append-only. Green required CI on the VERSION COMMIT still\n    20\t# comes from the push-to-main run after merge; close + reopen remains the operator path to force the\n    21\t# full pre-merge CI signal.\n    22\t#\n    23\t# The \"never in-branch `changeset version`\" rule (ADR-0321) is unchanged — this automation-authored\n    24\t# PR is the gated consumption point; it is still never a feature-branch act.\n    25\ton:\n    26\t  workflow_dispatch:\n    27\t  # Trusted-base synchronize hook: the workflow definition + executable tooling come from main.\n    28\t  # The PR head is checked out separately and treated only as data (never imported/executed).\n    29\t  pull_request_target:\n    30\t    branches: [main]\n    31\t    types: [synchronize]\n    32\t\n    33\tpermissions:\n    34\t  contents: read\n    35\t\n    36\tconcurrency:\n    37\t  group: version-pr-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || 'dispatch' }}\n    38\t  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request_target' }}\n    39\t\n    40\tjobs:\n    41\t  version-pr:\n    42\t    if: github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'\n    43\t    # Blacksmith per ADR-0365 (the 2026-07-19 fleet-only sweep; write perms accepted on VM-per-job runners).\n    44\t    # Write privilege belongs on a clean hosted runner, not third-party compute.\n    45\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    46\t    timeout-minutes: 15\n    47\t    environment: release # ADR-0327 rider 2: the release-family boundary (definition-first; free-plan protection rules can't enforce yet)\n    48\t    permissions:\n    49\t      contents: write\n    50\t      pull-requests: write\n    51\t    steps:\n    52\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n    53\t        with:\n    54\t          # Full history so changesets can read tags and the ledger diff is honest.\n    55\t          fetch-depth: 0\n    56\t      - uses: ./.github/actions/setup-bun\n    57\t      - run: bun install --frozen-lockfile\n    58\t      # Loud guard: dispatching with nothing to version is an operator mistake, not a no-op.\n    59\t      - name: require pending changesets\n    60\t        run: |\n    61\t          pending=\"$(find .changeset -maxdepth 1 -name '*.md' ! -name 'README.md' | wc -l)\"\n    62\t          if [ \"$pending\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    63\t            echo \"::error::no pending .changeset/*.md — nothing to version. Land changesets first.\"\n    64\t            exit 1\n    65\t          fi\n    66\t          echo \"[version-pr] $pending pending changeset(s)\"\n    67\t      - name: changeset version (consume)\n    68\t        run: bunx changeset version\n    69\t      # The generated component manifest embeds @caisson/ui's package version. Refresh it after\n    70\t      # Changesets bumps package.json so the version PR cannot ship stale design metadata.\n    71\t      - name: regenerate version-coupled design manifest\n    72\t        run: bun run --filter @caisson/ui gen:manifest\n    73\t      # The bumps change workspace package versions recorded in bun.lock — refresh it here (NOT\n    74\t      # frozen) so the merge commit passes every `bun install --frozen-lockfile` gate downstream.\n    75\t      - name: refresh bun.lock for the bumped versions\n    76\t        run: bun install\n    77\t      # Ledger append + index rebuild + tarball pack/hash rows — all INTO this PR (version mode\n    78\t      # writes tracked files; publish mode later verifies against them at the tag). The recorded\n    79\t      # gateAttestation is \"<run-id>@<base-sha>\" — the main SHA this PR was cut from; the release\n    80\t      # tag anchors the final merged state (a commit cannot contain its own SHA).\n    81\t      - name: append ledger + rebuild index + record tarball rows (version mode)\n    82\t        run: |\n    83\t          bun registry/scripts/ci-publish-step.ts \\\n    84\t            --mode version \\\n    85\t            --run-id \"${{ github.run_id }}\" \\\n    86\t            --sha \"${{ github.sha }}\" \\\n    87\t            --published-at \"$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.000Z')\" \\\n    88\t            --dry-run false\n    89\t      # Commit everything the consume produced and open the PR. Pathspecs cover EVERY workspace\n    90\t      # (apps/services/registry/tooling get dependent bumps too) + bun.lock; the loud leftovers\n    91\t      # check fails with filenames if a future write-site slips past the pathspec.\n    92\t      # registry/.tarball-staging/ is untracked and never staged.\n    93\t      - name: open the version PR\n    94\t        env:\n    95\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n    96\t        run: |\n    97\t          set -euo pipefail\n    98\t          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n    99\t          git config user.email \"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n   100\t          branch=\"release/version-${{ github.run_id }}\"\n   101\t          git switch -c \"$branch\"\n   102\t          git add -A -- \\\n   103\t            ':(glob)**/package.json' ':(glob)**/CHANGELOG.md' '.changeset' bun.lock \\\n   104\t            packages/ds-manifest/src/base-manifest.json \\\n   105\t            registry/ledger.jsonl registry/index.json registry/tarballs.json\n   106\t          if git diff --cached --quiet; then\n   107\t            echo \"::error::changeset version produced no changes — nothing to PR\"\n   108\t            exit 1\n   109\t          fi\n   110\t          if ! git diff --quiet; then\n   111\t            echo \"::error::tracked changes left unstaged after the pathspec add:\"\n   112\t            git status --short\n   113\t            exit 1\n   114\t          fi\n   115\t          git commit -m \"chore(release): version PR - consume changesets + ledger/index/tarball rows [version-pr]\"\n   116\t          git push -u origin \"$branch\"\n   117\t          gh pr create \\\n   118\t            --title \"chore(release): version PR ($(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d'), run ${{ github.run_id }})\" \\\n   119\t            --body \"$(printf '%s\\n' \\\n   120\t              \"Automation-authored version PR (ADR-0325). Contains the complete release source truth:\" \\\n   121\t              \"\" \\\n   122\t              \"- \\`changeset version\\` consume: package.json bumps + CHANGELOGs + drained \\`.changeset/\\`\" \\\n   123\t              \"- refreshed \\`bun.lock\\`\" \\\n   124\t              \"- \\`registry/ledger.jsonl\\` append + \\`registry/index.json\\` rebuild + \\`registry/tarballs.json\\` hash rows\" \\\n   125\t              \"\" \\\n   126\t              \"Next steps (release runbook):\" \\\n   127\t              \"1. Merge this PR (push-to-main CI runs the 5 required checks on the merge commit; this PR shows no checks because GITHUB_TOKEN pushes never trigger CI — close/reopen to force a pre-merge run).\" \\\n   128\t              \"2. Publish a GitHub Release whose tag targets EXACTLY the merge commit.\" \\\n   129\t              \"3. The release train verifies readiness and publishes the tagged bytes with zero mutation.\" \\\n   130\t              )\"\n   131\t\n   132\t  refresh-version-tarballs:\n   133\t    # Same-repo automation release branches only. Fork PRs never receive write authority, and the\n   134\t    # trusted main copy of this workflow never executes candidate source or lifecycle scripts.\n   135\t    if: >-\n   136\t      github.event_name == 'pull_request_target' &&\n   137\t      github.event.pull_request.base.ref == 'main' &&\n   138\t      github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository &&\n   139\t      startsWith(github.event.pull_request.head.ref, 'release/version-')\n   140\t    # Blacksmith per ADR-0365 (fleet-only sweep; release-branch write accepted on VM-per-job runners).\n   141\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n   142\t    timeout-minutes: 15\n   143\t    environment: release\n   144\t    permissions:\n   145\t      contents: write\n   146\t      pull-requests: read\n   147\t    steps:\n   148\t      - name: checkout trusted base tooling\n   149\t        uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n   150\t        with:\n   151\t          fetch-depth: 1\n   152\t          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}\n   153\t          path: trusted\n   154\t          persist-credentials: false\n   155\t      - name: checkout candidate release branch as data only\n   156\t        uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n   157\t        with:\n   158\t          fetch-depth: 0\n   159\t          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}\n   160\t          path: candidate\n   161\t          persist-credentials: false\n   162\t      - uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@0c5077e51419868618aeaa5fe8019c62421857d6 # v2.2.0\n   163\t        with:\n   164\t          bun-version: \"1.4.2\"\n   165\t      - name: cache bun installs\n   166\t        uses: actions/cache@55cc8345863c7cc4c66a329aec7e433d2d1c52a9 # v6\n   167\t        with:\n   168\t          path: ~/.bun/install/cache\n   169\t          key: ${{ runner.os }}-bun-${{ hashFiles('trusted/bun.lock', 'candidate/bun.lock') }}\n   170\t          restore-keys: ${{ runner.os }}-bun-\n   171\t      - name: install trusted base dependencies without lifecycle scripts\n   172\t        working-directory: trusted\n   173\t        run: bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts\n   174\t      # Materialize the candidate's dependency graph under its own committed lockfile so `bun pm\n   175\t      # pack` rewrites workspace dependencies from candidate resolution. `--ignore-scripts` keeps\n   176\t      # the PR head data-only: no candidate lifecycle hook executes; the packer/tooling stays trusted.\n   177\t      - name: install candidate dependencies under its frozen lockfile without lifecycle scripts\n   178\t        working-directory: candidate\n   179\t        run: bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts\n   180\t      - name: re-record unmerged version-branch tarball rows\n   181\t        run: |\n   182\t          set -euo pipefail\n   183\t          base_sha=\"$(git -C candidate merge-base HEAD '${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}')\"\n   184\t          base_sidecar=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/base-tarballs.json\"\n   185\t          base_ledger=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/base-ledger.jsonl\"\n   186\t          git -C candidate show \"${base_sha}:registry/tarballs.json\" > \"$base_sidecar\"\n   187\t          git -C candidate show \"${base_sha}:registry/ledger.jsonl\" > \"$base_ledger\"\n   188\t          bun trusted/registry/scripts/ci-publish-step.ts \\\n   189\t            --refresh-candidate-root \"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/candidate\" \\\n   190\t            --refresh-base-sidecar \"$base_sidecar\" \\\n   191\t            --refresh-base-ledger \"$base_ledger\" \\\n   192\t            --dry-run false\n   193\t      - name: commit refreshed release truth when bytes changed\n   194\t        env:\n   195\t          HEAD_REF: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.ref }}\n   196\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n   197\t        run: |\n   198\t          set -euo pipefail\n   199\t          if git -C candidate diff --quiet -- registry/tarballs.json; then\n   200\t            echo \"[version-pr] tarball rows already reproduce the branch source\"\n   201\t            exit 0\n   202\t          fi\n   203\t          git -C candidate config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n   204\t          git -C candidate config user.email \"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n   205\t          git -C candidate add -- registry/tarballs.json\n   206\t          changed=\"$(git -C candidate diff --cached --name-only)\"\n   207\t          if [ \"$changed\" != \"registry/tarballs.json\" ]; then\n   208\t            echo \"::error::trusted refresh produced an unexpected staged path: $changed\"\n   209\t            exit 1\n   210\t          fi\n   211\t          git -C candidate commit -m \"chore(release): refresh version-branch tarball rows [version-pr-refresh]\"\n   212\t          basic=\"$(printf 'x-access-token:%s' \"$GH_TOKEN\" | base64 -w0)\"\n   213\t          git -C candidate \\\n   214\t            -c http.https://github.com/.extraheader=\"AUTHORIZATION: basic $basic\" \\\n   215\t            push origin \"HEAD:${HEAD_REF}\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
