{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba .github/workflows/security-scan.yml'","aggregated_output":"     1\tname: security-scan\n     2\t# The deterministic security layer (SAST + supply-chain), split into its own workflow per the\n     3\t# ci.yml convention. REQUIRED since the ADR-0327 scan-gate flip (sequenced after the CAISSON-95\n     4\t# pinning in this same change): `deterministic` joins the required-check set — check ·\n     5\t# standards-gate · registry-index · oscal-conformance · deterministic (· support-bot, added by\n     6\t# ADR-0414 — see that workflow's header). As with the others,\n     7\t# \"required\" is discipline on this free-plan private repo (no enforced branch protection): the\n     8\t# convention is enforced by scripts/release-readiness.ts (REQUIRED_CHECKS) and review practice,\n     9\t# not a GitHub gate. `semgrep-pro` stays advisory (dormant until its token is provisioned).\n    10\t# Runs the repo-local tools/security/scan.sh — the same driver the operator runs locally.\n    11\t#\n    12\t# Scanner installs are version-pinned + digest-verified against tools/security/versions.env\n    13\t# (CAISSON-95) — no curl|sh from a moving main branch, no floating `latest`. The only third-party\n    14\t# marketplace action is the SHA-pinned astral-sh/setup-uv (same pin as support-bot.yml). No SARIF\n    15\t# upload to the GitHub Security tab — that needs Advanced Security, which this private free-plan\n    16\t# repo doesn't have; the SARIF set is saved as a downloadable artifact instead.\n    17\t#\n    18\t# The Semgrep PRO leg is a separate job gated on the SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN secret (a new external\n    19\t# egress sink to semgrep.dev — see identity/security-surfaces.md). It stays dormant until the\n    20\t# token is provisioned.\n    21\ton:\n    22\t  schedule:\n    23\t    # Daily 06:37 UTC on main; no image publication or registry credentials (R332).\n    24\t    - cron: \"37 6 * * *\"\n    25\t  push:\n    26\t    branches: [main]\n    27\t  pull_request:\n    28\t    # Defaults plus ready_for_review — flipping a draft to ready fires the full run (CAISSON-96).\n    29\t    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]\n    30\t\n    31\tconcurrency:\n    32\t  group: \"security-scan-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name }}-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.ref }}\"\n    33\t  cancel-in-progress: true\n    34\t\n    35\tpermissions:\n    36\t  contents: read\n    37\t\n    38\tjobs:\n    39\t  # Deterministic layer: semgrep floor rules + p/security-audit, ruff flake8-bandit (support-bot),\n    40\t  # trivy, osv-scanner, trufflehog (verified-only), Dockerfile digest gate (advisory). SEMGREP_JOBS=1\n    41\t  # dodges the semgrep-core io_uring crash the fleet box can hit under parallelism.\n    42\t  deterministic:\n    43\t    # CAISSON-96 draft guard — drafts skip; the ready_for_review trigger runs the full scan.\n    44\t    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\n    45\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    46\t    timeout-minutes: 20\n    47\t    env:\n    48\t      SEMGREP_JOBS: \"1\"\n    49\t      SEMGREP_SEND_METRICS: \"off\"\n    50\t    steps:\n    51\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n    52\t        with:\n    53\t          fetch-depth: 0 # trufflehog git-history scan needs full history\n    54\t          persist-credentials: false\n    55\t      - uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@11f9893b081a58869d3b5fccaea48c9e9e46f990 # v8.3.2\n    56\t        with:\n    57\t          version: \"0.12.2\" # pinned (same pin as support-bot.yml; no drift)\n    58\t      - name: base rescan contract tests (offline)\n    59\t        run: python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tools/security -p test_*images.py -v\n    60\t      - name: runtime OS upgrade contract tests (offline)\n    61\t        run: python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tools/security -p test_runtime_os_patch.py -v\n    62\t      - name: install scanners (pinned versions, sha256-verified release artifacts)\n    63\t        id: scanners\n    64\t        run: |\n    65\t          # CAISSON-95: every scanner is version-pinned and digest-verified against\n    66\t          # tools/security/versions.env — the old `curl | sh` installers fetched their script from\n    67\t          # each project's MOVING main branch (an unauditable execution path), and the\n    68\t          # `command -v || install` guards would have silently accepted ANY preinstalled version.\n    69\t          # Installs are now unconditional (deterministic on a throwaway VM) and fail loud:\n    70\t          # pipefail + sha256sum -c mean a bad download or tampered artifact reddens the job.\n    71\t          # Every download retries (2026-08-12): a single transient 503 from GitHub's release CDN\n    72\t          # reddened this job twice in a row on PR #431, five minutes apart, while all three URLs\n    73\t          # served 200 from the operator box — runner-side egress, not the pins. Retrying costs\n    74\t          # nothing in integrity: `sha256sum -c` still verifies each artifact against versions.env,\n    75\t          # so a retry can only turn a transport failure into the same verified bytes or a red job.\n    76\t          set -eo pipefail\n    77\t          source tools/security/versions.env\n    78\t          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n    79\t          mkdir -p \"$HOME/.local/bin\"\n    80\t          uv tool install \"semgrep==${SEMGREP_VERSION}\"\n    81\t          uv tool install \"ruff==${RUFF_VERSION}\"\n    82\t          tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n    83\t          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/trivy.tgz\" \"https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/releases/download/v${TRIVY_VERSION}/trivy_${TRIVY_VERSION}_Linux-64bit.tar.gz\"\n    84\t          echo \"${TRIVY_SHA256}  $tmp/trivy.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -\n    85\t          tar -C \"$tmp\" -xzf \"$tmp/trivy.tgz\" trivy\n    86\t          install -m755 \"$tmp/trivy\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/trivy\"\n    87\t          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/trufflehog.tgz\" \"https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/releases/download/v${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}/trufflehog_${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}_linux_amd64.tar.gz\"\n    88\t          echo \"${TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256}  $tmp/trufflehog.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -\n    89\t          tar -C \"$tmp\" -xzf \"$tmp/trufflehog.tgz\" trufflehog\n    90\t          install -m755 \"$tmp/trufflehog\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/trufflehog\"\n    91\t          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/osv-scanner\" \"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/releases/download/v${OSV_SCANNER_VERSION}/osv-scanner_linux_amd64\"\n    92\t          echo \"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256}  $tmp/osv-scanner\" | sha256sum -c -\n    93\t          install -m755 \"$tmp/osv-scanner\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/osv-scanner\"\n    94\t          rm -rf \"$tmp\"\n    95\t          # Re-assert every tool resolved — a missing tool must hard-fail the job, never silent-skip.\n    96\t          for t in semgrep ruff trivy trufflehog osv-scanner; do\n    97\t            command -v \"$t\" >/dev/null || { echo \"::error::$t missing after install — scan layer would silently skip\"; exit 1; }\n    98\t          done\n    99\t      - name: security scan (SAST + supply-chain)\n   100\t        run: |\n   101\t          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n   102\t          # SARIF lands in $RUNNER_TEMP (OUT of the scanned tree) so `trivy fs .` never re-scans\n   103\t          # semgrep's freshly-written SARIF. Set at step scope: the `runner` context is unavailable\n   104\t          # in a job-level `env:`, and $RUNNER_TEMP is the shell form of it inside a step. The dir is\n   105\t          # deliberately NON-hidden: actions/upload-artifact@v4 (>=4.4) excludes hidden files/dirs by\n   106\t          # default, so a dot-dir uploaded empty (\"No files were found\") — the SARIF set evaporated.\n   107\t          export SECURITY_OUT_DIR=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/security-out\"\n   108\t          # --strict-digests: Dockerfile digest-pin check (K-03) is ENFORCING — the ADR-0315\n   109\t          # trigger (Renovate's first pin-wave merged) fired 2026-07-13; check-docker-digests.sh\n   110\t          # proven green on main 2026-07-17 before the flip.\n   111\t          bash tools/security/scan.sh --layer ci --strict-digests\n   112\t      - name: report raw Dockerfile base digests (informational, anonymous)\n   113\t        if: ${{ !cancelled() && steps.scanners.outcome == 'success' }}\n   114\t        continue-on-error: true # R335: raw-base results never gate the job.\n   115\t        run: |\n   116\t          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n   117\t          python3 tools/security/rescan_base_images.py --output \"$RUNNER_TEMP/security-out\"\n   118\t      - name: upload SARIF artifacts\n   119\t        if: always()\n   120\t        uses: actions/upload-artifact@043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a # v7\n   121\t        with:\n   122\t          name: security-sarif-${{ github.sha }}\n   123\t          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/security-out\n   124\t          if-no-files-found: warn\n   125\t          retention-days: 30\n   126\t\n   127\t  # Semgrep PRO (interfile / cross-function taint). Dormant until SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN is set. The job\n   128\t  # ALWAYS runs — a job-level `if` CANNOT reference the `secrets` context (doing so is a parse-time\n   129\t  # \"Unrecognized named-value: secrets\" that invalidates the ENTIRE workflow file, killing the\n   130\t  # deterministic job too) — but the single step below no-ops without a token. `semgrep ci`\n   131\t  # self-authenticates from the token and pulls the org policy rules. SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN and\n   132\t  # SEMGREP_RULES are mutually exclusive — never set both.\n   133\t  semgrep-pro:\n   134\t    # CAISSON-96 draft guard — drafts skip; the ready_for_review trigger runs the full scan.\n   135\t    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\n   136\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n   137\t    # 45, not 20: this job's runtime swings hard. On 2026-07-27 it hit the old 20-minute ceiling on\n   138\t    # `87202cd9` and then passed in ~3 minutes on an immediate re-run of the identical tree — a 7x\n   139\t    # spread. A timed-out job reports as `cancelled`, which reads like someone aborted it rather\n   140\t    # than a scan that never finished, and because this check is advisory nothing forced anyone to\n   141\t    # look. The ceiling now sits above the observed worst case so the result means something.\n   142\t    #\n   143\t    # NOT changed here: the `-j 1` below (and its SEMGREP_JOBS twin). Single-threading is a\n   144\t    # deliberate workaround for a semgrep-core io_uring crash, and that comment was written about\n   145\t    # the self-hosted fleet box — this job runs on a 4-vCPU Blacksmith VM, so the workaround may not\n   146\t    # apply and is likely the bulk of the runtime. Worth testing, but not worth guessing at inside a\n   147\t    # launch deploy: removing a crash workaround on inference is how you trade a slow check for a\n   148\t    # flaky one.\n   149\t    timeout-minutes: 45\n   150\t    env:\n   151\t      SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN }}\n   152\t      SEMGREP_JOBS: \"1\"\n   153\t    steps:\n   154\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n   155\t      - uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@11f9893b081a58869d3b5fccaea48c9e9e46f990 # v8.3.2\n   156\t        with:\n   157\t          version: \"0.12.2\" # pinned (same pin as support-bot.yml; no drift)\n   158\t      # One guarded step: skip cleanly (installing nothing) when the token is absent; otherwise\n   159\t      # install the PINNED semgrep (CAISSON-95, tools/security/versions.env) and run the Pro\n   160\t      # platform-policy scan (interfile/cross-function taint). The custom floor rules run in the\n   161\t      # `deterministic` job (pattern rules need no Pro engine); add them to the Semgrep policy to\n   162\t      # have them Pro-analyzed too.\n   163\t      - name: semgrep ci (Pro cross-file taint) — dormant until SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN is set\n   164\t        run: |\n   165\t          if [ -z \"${SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN:-}\" ]; then\n   166\t            echo \"SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN not set — Pro scan skipped (provision the repo secret to activate)\"\n   167\t            exit 0\n   168\t          fi\n   169\t          set -eo pipefail\n   170\t          source tools/security/versions.env\n   171\t          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n   172\t          uv tool install \"semgrep==${SEMGREP_VERSION}\"\n   173\t          semgrep ci -j 1\n   174\t\n   175\t  # zizmor — GitHub Actions workflow auditor (Kickoff T task 2). ADVISORY for now: SARIF mode\n   176\t  # always exits 0 (findings live in the SARIF, not the exit code), so this job can never block\n   177\t  # a merge. Gate ramp: once the finding set is triaged to zero-or-ignored (zizmor.yml `ignore`\n   178\t  # entries with rationale), drop `--no-exit-codes`, switch --format to plain, and add the job to\n   179\t  # the required-check convention in scripts/release-readiness.ts — the repo is already SHA-pinned\n   180\t  # throughout, so the steady-state finding rate should be near zero. Same pinned-install\n   181\t  # discipline as the deterministic job: version + sha256 from tools/security/versions.env\n   182\t  # (zizmor releases attach no checksums file — the pinned digest was verified by local download,\n   183\t  # see versions.env comment).\n   184\t  zizmor:\n   185\t    # CAISSON-96 draft guard — drafts skip; the ready_for_review trigger runs the full scan.\n   186\t    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\n   187\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n   188\t    timeout-minutes: 10\n   189\t    steps:\n   190\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n   191\t      - name: install zizmor (pinned version, sha256-verified release artifact)\n   192\t        run: |\n   193\t          set -eo pipefail\n   194\t          source tools/security/versions.env\n   195\t          mkdir -p \"$HOME/.local/bin\"\n   196\t          tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n   197\t          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/zizmor.tgz\" \"https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/releases/download/v${ZIZMOR_VERSION}/zizmor-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz\"\n   198\t          echo \"${ZIZMOR_SHA256}  $tmp/zizmor.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -\n   199\t          tar -C \"$tmp\" -xzf \"$tmp/zizmor.tgz\"\n   200\t          find \"$tmp\" -name zizmor -type f -exec install -m755 {} \"$HOME/.local/bin/zizmor\" \\;\n   201\t          rm -rf \"$tmp\"\n   202\t          command -v \"$HOME/.local/bin/zizmor\" >/dev/null || { echo \"::error::zizmor missing after install\"; exit 1; }\n   203\t      - name: zizmor audit (advisory — SARIF artifact, never blocks)\n   204\t        env:\n   205\t          # Online audits (impostor-commit, ref-confusion, stale-action-refs) need read access to\n   206\t          # public commit graphs; the default token's `contents: read` suffices.\n   207\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n   208\t        run: |\n   209\t          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n   210\t          mkdir -p \"$RUNNER_TEMP/zizmor-out\"\n   211\t          zizmor --persona=regular --format=sarif --no-exit-codes .github/workflows/ > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/zizmor-out/zizmor.sarif\"\n   212\t          # Human-readable echo for the job log (advisory visibility without downloading the SARIF).\n   213\t          zizmor --persona=regular --no-exit-codes .github/workflows/ || true\n   214\t      - name: upload zizmor SARIF artifact\n   215\t        if: always()\n   216\t        uses: actions/upload-artifact@043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a # v7\n   217\t        with:\n   218\t          name: zizmor-sarif-${{ github.sha }}\n   219\t          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/zizmor-out\n   220\t          if-no-files-found: warn\n   221\t          retention-days: 30\n   222\t\n   223\t  runtime-select:\n   224\t    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\n   225\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n   226\t    outputs:\n   227\t      matrix: ${{ steps.select.outputs.matrix }}\n   228\t    steps:\n   229\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n   230\t        with:\n   231\t          persist-credentials: false\n   232\t      - id: select\n   233\t        run: |\n   234\t          matrix=\"$(python3 -B tools/security/rescan_runtime_images.py --matrix)\"\n   235\t          printf 'matrix=%s\\n' \"$matrix\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n   236\t\n   237\t  runtime-images:\n   238\t    name: runtime image (${{ matrix.name }})\n   239\t    needs: runtime-select\n   240\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n   241\t    timeout-minutes: 35\n   242\t    strategy:\n   243\t      fail-fast: false\n   244\t      max-parallel: 4\n   245\t      matrix: ${{ fromJSON(needs.runtime-select.outputs.matrix) }}\n   246\t    env:\n   247\t      IMAGE: caisson-runtime-rescan:${{ matrix.name }}\n   248\t    steps:\n   249\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n   250\t        with:\n   251\t          persist-credentials: false\n   252\t      - name: prepare disposable runner disk\n   253\t        run: |\n   254\t          # Same fixed SDK set proven by PR 483. This job needs its own cleanup\n   255\t          # before that sibling PR merges; neither PR may merge independently (R336).\n   256\t          df -B1 / \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n   257\t          sudo rm -rf -- /usr/local/lib/android /usr/local/.ghcup /usr/local/swift /usr/share/dotnet\n   258\t          df -B1 / \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n   259\t      - name: install pinned Trivy\n   260\t        run: |\n   261\t          set -euo pipefail\n   262\t          source tools/security/versions.env\n   263\t          tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n   264\t          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/trivy.tgz\" \"https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/releases/download/v${TRIVY_VERSION}/trivy_${TRIVY_VERSION}_Linux-64bit.tar.gz\"\n   265\t          echo \"${TRIVY_SHA256}  $tmp/trivy.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -\n   266\t          tar -C \"$tmp\" -xzf \"$tmp/trivy.tgz\" trivy\n   267\t          mkdir -p \"$HOME/.local/bin\"\n   268\t          install -m755 \"$tmp/trivy\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/trivy\"\n   269\t          echo \"$HOME/.local/bin\" >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"\n   270\t      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@37fe631027851001ddb9b187196cc803df7f5f0e # v4.3.0\n   271\t      - name: build patched runtime (no publish)\n   272\t        uses: docker/build-push-action@53b7df96c91f9c12dcc8a07bcb9ccacbed38856a # v7.3.0\n   273\t        with:\n   274\t          context: ${{ matrix.context }}\n   275\t          file: ${{ matrix.dockerfile }}\n   276\t          target: ${{ matrix.target }}\n   277\t          platforms: linux/amd64\n   278\t          no-cache: true # Execute apt update/upgrade on every scheduled rebuild.\n   279\t          pull: true\n   280\t          push: false\n   281\t          load: true\n   282\t          tags: ${{ env.IMAGE }}\n   283\t      - name: record built image provenance\n   284\t        env:\n   285\t          DOCKERFILE: ${{ matrix.dockerfile }}\n   286\t          TARGET: ${{ matrix.target }}\n   287\t        run: |\n   288\t          mkdir -p \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan\"\n   289\t          git rev-parse HEAD > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/source-sha.txt\"\n   290\t          printf '%s\\n' \"$DOCKERFILE\" \"$TARGET\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/build-target.txt\"\n   291\t          docker image inspect \"$IMAGE\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/image-inspect.json\"\n   292\t          df -B1 / \"$RUNNER_TEMP\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/disk-before.txt\"\n   293\t      - name: enforce runtime OS vulnerabilities and report application residual\n   294\t        run: python3 -B tools/security/rescan_runtime_images.py --image \"$IMAGE\" --output \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/image.json\"\n   295\t      - name: upload runtime reports and application/unfixed residuals\n   296\t        if: always()\n   297\t        uses: actions/upload-artifact@043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a # v7\n   298\t        with:\n   299\t          name: runtime-rescan-${{ matrix.name }}\n   300\t          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/runtime-scan\n   301\t          if-no-files-found: error\n   302\t          retention-days: 30\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
